2026-07-10T11:50:38.2283823Z     
2026-07-10T11:50:38.2284084Z     The ``pytest`` framework makes it easy to write small tests, yet
2026-07-10T11:50:38.2284563Z     scales to support complex functional testing for applications and libraries.
2026-07-10T11:50:38.2284960Z     
2026-07-10T11:50:38.2285151Z     An example of a simple test:
2026-07-10T11:50:38.2285389Z     
2026-07-10T11:50:38.2285574Z     .. code-block:: python
2026-07-10T11:50:38.2285801Z     
2026-07-10T11:50:38.2285992Z         # content of test_sample.py
2026-07-10T11:50:38.2286242Z         def inc(x):
2026-07-10T11:50:38.2286445Z             return x + 1
2026-07-10T11:50:38.2286660Z     
2026-07-10T11:50:38.2286829Z     
2026-07-10T11:50:38.2287019Z         def test_answer():
2026-07-10T11:50:38.2287254Z             assert inc(3) == 5
2026-07-10T11:50:38.2287477Z     
2026-07-10T11:50:38.2287647Z     
2026-07-10T11:50:38.2287828Z     To execute it::
2026-07-10T11:50:38.2288029Z     
2026-07-10T11:50:38.2288206Z         $ pytest
2026-07-10T11:50:38.2288595Z         ============================= test session starts =============================
2026-07-10T11:50:38.2288944Z         collected 1 items
2026-07-10T11:50:38.2289172Z     
2026-07-10T11:50:38.2289481Z         test_sample.py F
2026-07-10T11:50:38.2289701Z     
2026-07-10T11:50:38.2289940Z         ================================== FAILURES ===================================
2026-07-10T11:50:38.2290107Z         _________________________________ test_answer _________________________________
2026-07-10T11:50:38.2290184Z     
2026-07-10T11:50:38.2290325Z             def test_answer():
2026-07-10T11:50:38.2297752Z         >       assert inc(3) == 5
2026-07-10T11:50:38.2297895Z         E       assert 4 == 5
2026-07-10T11:50:38.2297993Z         E        +  where 4 = inc(3)
2026-07-10T11:50:38.2298074Z     
2026-07-10T11:50:38.2298188Z         test_sample.py:5: AssertionError
2026-07-10T11:50:38.2298666Z         ========================== 1 failed in 0.04 seconds ===========================
2026-07-10T11:50:38.2298826Z     
2026-07-10T11:50:38.2298965Z     
2026-07-10T11:50:38.2299766Z     Thanks to ``pytest``'s detailed assertion introspection, you can simply use plain ``assert`` statements. See `getting-started <https://docs.pytest.org/en/stable/getting-started.html#our-first-test-run>`_ for more examples.
2026-07-10T11:50:38.2300055Z     
2026-07-10T11:50:38.2300135Z     
2026-07-10T11:50:38.2300222Z     Features
2026-07-10T11:50:38.2300308Z     --------
2026-07-10T11:50:38.2300383Z     
2026-07-10T11:50:38.2300865Z     - Detailed info on failing `assert statements <https://docs.pytest.org/en/stable/how-to/assert.html>`_ (no need to remember ``self.assert*`` names)
2026-07-10T11:50:38.2300945Z     
2026-07-10T11:50:38.2301038Z     - `Auto-discovery
2026-07-10T11:50:38.2301334Z       <https://docs.pytest.org/en/stable/explanation/goodpractices.html#python-test-discovery>`_
2026-07-10T11:50:38.2301441Z       of test modules and functions
2026-07-10T11:50:38.2301515Z     
2026-07-10T11:50:38.2301781Z     - `Modular fixtures <https://docs.pytest.org/en/stable/explanation/fixtures.html>`_ for
2026-07-10T11:50:38.2301953Z       managing small or parametrized long-lived test resources
2026-07-10T11:50:38.2302036Z     
2026-07-10T11:50:38.2302303Z     - Can run `unittest <https://docs.pytest.org/en/stable/how-to/unittest.html>`_ (or trial)
2026-07-10T11:50:38.2302405Z       test suites out of the box
2026-07-10T11:50:38.2302479Z     
2026-07-10T11:50:38.2302579Z     - Python 3.10+ or PyPy3
2026-07-10T11:50:38.2302659Z     
2026-07-10T11:50:38.2303123Z     - Rich plugin architecture, with over 1300+ `external plugins <https://docs.pytest.org/en/latest/reference/plugin_list.html>`_ and thriving community
